-- check/bad: §10.11 and §6.4. 65 distinct methods on one unannotated
-- declaration, one over `Solver.max_inferred_constraints`. The cap exists so
-- that neither the inferred `where` suffix (report 19 §3.1: a 6.4 kB interface
-- entry is reachable) nor the n(n+1)/2 an unannotated chain accumulates
-- (report 19 §3) is unbounded. Only the first five names are printed: bounding
-- the message is half the point.
--
-- The twins are `check/good/SixtyFourConstraints.beni` (64, accepted) and
-- `check/good/AnnotatedManyConstraints.beni` (65 in a `where` clause the
-- author wrote, accepted — an annotation lifts the cap).
